   <p>
    I don't know in what book I
    once read. (probably the remark has
    been made in books all ages.) that no
    life ever lived, even the most uneventful,
    but probed to its centre would be
    found a subtler drama in itself that
    poets yet have sung or playwrights fabled.
    Often, too, in real size and weight. It
    isn't only the visible orbs astronomers
    say, there are dark or almost dark stars
    and suns.
   </p>
   
